{\an8}<i>♪ Mmm-hmm, right ♪</i>

25
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
EAT MY VOW

26
00:01:37,107 --> 00:01:40,319
[Legoshi] Here you go.
Tsukimi Udon with extra dandelion.

27
00:01:40,402 --> 00:01:41,529
[Haru] Wow! [chuckles]

28
00:01:42,863 --> 00:01:44,949
Mmm. Smells good.

29
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:48,285
Hey, you got a sec to sit down?

30
00:01:48,369 --> 00:01:49,203
Uh...

31
00:01:49,662 --> 00:01:51,831
Well, is that okay with you?

32
00:01:51,914 --> 00:01:53,582
She was my senior in high school.

33
00:01:53,666 --> 00:01:55,835
Legoshi, you've got yourself a girlfriend?

34
00:01:55,918 --> 00:01:57,586
- Uh...
- [both chuckle]

35
00:02:00,798 --> 00:02:03,217
Well, hey, thanks for coming out
for my birthday.

36
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:05,845
Yeah, of course. I wanted to see you.

37
00:02:05,928 --> 00:02:09,682
Plus, I was curious to see what kind
of place was lucky enough to hire you.

38
00:02:09,765 --> 00:02:12,226
It's cute. And I like the seats
for small animals.

39
00:02:12,309 --> 00:02:13,352
[Legoshi] Mmm.

40
00:02:13,435 --> 00:02:14,770
Thanks for the food!

41
00:02:15,479 --> 00:02:16,730
- Ah!
- What?

42
00:02:16,814 --> 00:02:19,275
Uh, nothing. I just think that
that's a good idea,

43
00:02:19,358 --> 00:02:21,443
breaking up the egg in the noodles first.

44
00:02:21,527 --> 00:02:23,737
What? You don't do that?
You're missing out.

45
00:02:23,821 --> 00:02:25,656
It's served in the same bowl for a reason.

46
00:02:25,739 --> 00:02:26,740
[Legoshi] Mmm.

47
00:02:27,575 --> 00:02:30,119
[blowing]

48
00:02:31,787 --> 00:02:32,830
[slurps]

49
00:02:32,913 --> 00:02:35,332
[chews, gulps]

50
00:02:36,083 --> 00:02:37,126
This is delicious!

51
00:02:37,209 --> 00:02:38,377
[Legoshi laughs]

52
00:02:39,378 --> 00:02:42,506
[blowing, slurps]

53
00:02:43,090 --> 00:02:44,717
[Haru chuckles]

54
00:02:46,594 --> 00:02:48,512
- [Haru slurps]
- Haru.

55
00:02:50,306 --> 00:02:52,182
There's something I need to tell you.

56
00:02:53,142 --> 00:02:56,353
I... I wanted to say this
at the bus station, but...

57
00:02:57,813 --> 00:02:58,772
Can I tell you now?

58
00:02:59,315 --> 00:03:00,441
Mmm?

59
00:03:00,524 --> 00:03:02,484
The reason I dropped out of school...

60
00:03:02,568 --> 00:03:03,527
[slurps]

61
00:03:04,778 --> 00:03:07,239
Well, it's because I ate Louis' right leg.

62
00:03:07,323 --> 00:03:09,158
[Haru sighs] Really?

63
00:03:09,241 --> 00:03:11,410
[sighs] I'm trying to eat here, you know?

64
00:03:11,493 --> 00:03:13,120
- Huh?
- [Haru grunting]

65
00:03:13,203 --> 00:03:15,706
- Uh... [splutters] Hey. Haru, were are you--
- [Haru grunting]

66
00:03:15,789 --> 00:03:16,624
Hmm?

67
00:03:19,209 --> 00:03:20,419
- Present time.
- What?

68
00:03:20,502 --> 00:03:23,005
We are going to buy you
a birthday present, okay?

69
00:03:23,088 --> 00:03:25,174
You can tell me more about it on the way.

70
00:03:26,008 --> 00:03:28,052
- While we're on our date!
- Uh--

71
00:03:28,719 --> 00:03:29,678
Uh...

72
00:03:29,762 --> 00:03:32,848
- You can take off early today.
- [Legoshi chuckles nervously]

73
00:03:33,641 --> 00:03:35,684
[pleasant music playing]

74
00:03:38,187 --> 00:03:39,939
Oh, look at the dinosaurs!

75
00:03:40,022 --> 00:03:42,024
- Hmm? Yeah. Uh...
- Which one do you want?

76
00:03:42,107 --> 00:03:43,734
[Haru] Wow, they're huge!

77
00:03:43,817 --> 00:03:45,110
Look at that one.

78
00:03:45,194 --> 00:03:48,656
- Some were even bigger. Yeah.
- Yeah? I never knew that.

79
00:03:48,739 --> 00:03:50,199
[Haru pants]

80
00:03:50,282 --> 00:03:52,910
- Over here! How do I look?
- [Legoshi chuckles] You look good.

81
00:03:52,993 --> 00:03:55,371
<i>I told her everything. I had to.</i>

82
00:03:55,454 --> 00:03:56,580
- Open your mouth.
- That mine?

83
00:03:56,664 --> 00:03:59,583
<i>I told her about the fight with Riz
after I found him out.</i>

84
00:04:00,292 --> 00:04:03,170
<i>I told her how I ate Louis' leg,
with his permission,</i>

85
00:04:03,254 --> 00:04:05,422
<i>in a desperate attempt to win that fight.</i>

86
00:04:05,506 --> 00:04:07,967
[Haru] Wow. That was enough
to cause withdrawal?

87
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:12,513
Mmm. Sometimes I can't control myself
when I come into contact with herbivores.

88
00:04:13,264 --> 00:04:15,641
Oh, but I-- I'm fine right now. I promise.

89
00:04:15,724 --> 00:04:18,644
Hmm. Then, how about some mint?

90
00:04:18,727 --> 00:04:20,312
- Hmm?
- It has a relaxing effect.

91
00:04:21,438 --> 00:04:23,315
I didn't know that. Hmm.

92
00:04:26,235 --> 00:04:29,405
[Haru] <i>I've always tried
to stay out of Legoshi's business.</i>

93
00:04:30,489 --> 00:04:32,324
<i>I never asked what he was up to.</i>

94
00:04:33,033 --> 00:04:35,703
<i>Hmm. Maybe I was too scared to find out.</i>

95
00:04:36,287 --> 00:04:38,998
Hmm. That is nice.

96
00:04:46,672 --> 00:04:49,133
Look! It's the Cherryton windmill.

97
00:04:49,925 --> 00:04:52,678
And that's where
you pulled out your fangs, right?

98
00:04:52,761 --> 00:04:53,804
[Legoshi] Mmm.

99
00:04:53,887 --> 00:04:56,473
- Yeah, somewhere around there. Yeah.
- [chuckles]

100
00:04:58,517 --> 00:04:59,977
[Haru sighs deeply]

101
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:02,396
This sucks, though. This big old fence.

102
00:05:02,479 --> 00:05:03,981
Well, they have to have it.

103
00:05:04,064 --> 00:05:07,359
Imagine if there was an incident
while someone was up in the air.

104
00:05:07,443 --> 00:05:09,737
I know that, but it ruins the mood.

105
00:05:10,988 --> 00:05:12,281
You really feel that way?

106
00:05:13,282 --> 00:05:15,492
- You're not just being nice?
- What?

107
00:05:16,618 --> 00:05:20,789
I know he said I could,
but I did still eat a person's leg.

108
00:05:22,124 --> 00:05:24,752
That has to change
how you see me. Doesn't it?

109
00:05:25,669 --> 00:05:26,628
Hmm...

110
00:05:28,005 --> 00:05:29,590
I guess I could scream and cry,

111
00:05:29,673 --> 00:05:31,967
or curse you out
if you really wanted me to.

112
00:05:32,051 --> 00:05:35,512
But, I don't know,
maybe you've had enough of that already.

113
00:05:38,515 --> 00:05:42,853
And I don't care anyway.
Our relationship is just ours.

114
00:05:44,271 --> 00:05:47,357
I have no intention of meddling
in your friendship with Louis.

115
00:05:48,609 --> 00:05:52,321
And my life hasn't been noble enough
for me to criticize you for anything.

116
00:05:54,865 --> 00:05:57,576
For carnivores and herbivores
to understand each other,

117
00:05:58,619 --> 00:06:00,913
we need to face each other with open eyes.

118
00:06:02,331 --> 00:06:05,542
And hearts.
So, that's what I've decided to do.

119
00:06:09,171 --> 00:06:12,800
And so, there's somewhere
I'd like to go together.

120
00:06:14,968 --> 00:06:16,303
- The market.
- What?

121
00:06:16,386 --> 00:06:19,139
- Take me to the Black Market.
- I can't do that.

122
00:06:19,223 --> 00:06:21,809
I want to know everything
about the boy I love.

123
00:06:22,935 --> 00:06:24,144
[Legoshi exhales softly]

124
00:06:25,062 --> 00:06:27,731
[Haru] So, is it a date?

125
00:06:31,193 --> 00:06:34,238
[Legoshi] Haru,
we really shouldn't do this.

126
00:06:34,947 --> 00:06:37,032
It's fine. I'm not scared.

127
00:06:37,116 --> 00:06:38,909
Uh-- Hey, stop for a second.

128
00:06:39,993 --> 00:06:40,994
[exclaims]

129
00:06:41,078 --> 00:06:43,455
- [muffled] What are you doing?
- At least hide your face.

130
00:06:43,539 --> 00:06:48,085
[exhales, grumbles] This is my favorite
sweater, and you've stretched it all out.

131
00:06:48,168 --> 00:06:50,671
I'm sorry, but your life
means more than a sweater.

132
00:06:50,754 --> 00:06:52,297
Oh, stop freaking out.

133
00:06:53,382 --> 00:06:55,843
[gasps] Now I can't see anything!

134
00:06:56,510 --> 00:06:58,637
[Haru groaning, grumbling]

135
00:06:59,805 --> 00:07:02,099
Come on! Ugh! Move your hand!

136
00:07:02,182 --> 00:07:03,433
- I--
- Sorry, but no.

137
00:07:03,517 --> 00:07:05,018
I can't see like this!

138
00:07:05,978 --> 00:07:07,980
[indistinct chattering]

139
00:07:08,981 --> 00:07:10,649
[upbeat music playing]

140
00:07:10,732 --> 00:07:12,734
Fresh cuts on sale! Step right up!

141
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:15,779
You okay?

142
00:07:16,488 --> 00:07:17,823
[gasps] Haru! Wait!

143
00:07:18,949 --> 00:07:21,493
{\an8}Hey, big guy. I bet you love a good deal!

144
00:07:21,577 --> 00:07:24,746
{\an8}- We got juicy mixed sausages for canines!
- Come and get your goat meat!

145
00:07:24,830 --> 00:07:29,042
{\an8}- We got legs, we got thighs, we got wings.
- [seller] Oh, if it isn't the young wolf.

146
00:07:29,126 --> 00:07:30,669
[Legoshi] Hey. It's been a while.

147
00:07:30,752 --> 00:07:33,255
I have fresh bamboo grass here,
if you'd like some.

148
00:07:33,338 --> 00:07:36,425
[Legoshi] Not today,
but maybe next time. [chuckles nervously]

149
00:07:37,009 --> 00:07:39,011
[sellers shouting indistinctly]

150
00:07:42,097 --> 00:07:45,642
- How about a bag of fresh rat?
- No, thank you. [gasps]

151
00:07:49,521 --> 00:07:50,731
[gasps, trembles]

152
00:07:50,814 --> 00:07:52,691
[slurps, grunts]

153
00:07:52,774 --> 00:07:55,152
Huh? [growling]

154
00:07:55,235 --> 00:07:56,487
[Haru panting]

155
00:07:57,613 --> 00:07:58,989
[customer panting]

156
00:07:59,907 --> 00:08:01,450
[Haru panting]

157
00:08:01,533 --> 00:08:03,035
[customer rapid panting]

158
00:08:03,118 --> 00:08:04,536
[Haru rapid panting]

159
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:05,954
[snarling]

160
00:08:06,622 --> 00:08:07,581
[Haru pants, gasps]

161
00:08:07,664 --> 00:08:10,792
Stay with me! Please,
you can't go running off like that.

162
00:08:13,045 --> 00:08:14,796
[grunts, scoffs]

163
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:16,548
Hey! Stop pulling!

164
00:08:17,299 --> 00:08:19,176
We should just go home--

165
00:08:20,052 --> 00:08:20,886
Haru?

166
00:08:26,266 --> 00:08:27,935
Haru.

167
00:08:28,018 --> 00:08:29,603
[whispers] It's dangerous here.

168
00:08:30,687 --> 00:08:32,147
- Over there.
- Hmm?

169
00:08:32,231 --> 00:08:33,482
RABBIT

170
00:08:33,565 --> 00:08:38,195
What? You can't be serious.
I-- Wait, wait, wait!

171
00:08:39,738 --> 00:08:45,369
RABBIT

172
00:08:53,085 --> 00:08:54,002
[Haru] You know...

173
00:08:54,962 --> 00:08:57,422
I hate myself for being
such a weak creature.

174
00:08:57,506 --> 00:08:59,591
Even if it is just an accident of birth.

175
00:09:00,509 --> 00:09:01,927
[sighs] I always have.

176
00:09:04,137 --> 00:09:06,181
That's why I wound up turning to sex.

177
00:09:07,975 --> 00:09:10,060
So, somehow, I came to decide

178
00:09:10,143 --> 00:09:12,729
that I could only be
someone's equal in bed.

179
00:09:14,147 --> 00:09:15,649
Pathetic. [sighs]

180
00:09:16,817 --> 00:09:18,527
I was was such a mess back then.

181
00:09:19,736 --> 00:09:21,655
I was barely keeping it together.

182
00:09:24,283 --> 00:09:25,367
But not now.

183
00:09:26,743 --> 00:09:29,413
Now, I'm safe.
I don't have to be reckless.

184
00:09:31,999 --> 00:09:33,625
Because now...

185
00:09:33,709 --> 00:09:35,252
I have you by my side.

186
00:09:35,335 --> 00:09:37,588
Um, my, uh...

187
00:09:37,671 --> 00:09:39,840
My stomach feels kind of weird.

188
00:09:39,923 --> 00:09:42,175
Don't go getting hungry
at a time like this.

189
00:09:42,259 --> 00:09:44,094
Yeah, you're surrounded by food,
but, come on!

190
00:09:44,177 --> 00:09:45,304
It's not that.

191
00:09:46,555 --> 00:09:47,472
Legoshi...

192
00:09:49,099 --> 00:09:50,100
will you kiss me?

193
00:09:51,685 --> 00:09:52,686
Right here?

194
00:09:54,021 --> 00:09:54,980
Please kiss me.

195
00:09:58,859 --> 00:10:00,777
Let go of everything else out there.

196
00:10:02,404 --> 00:10:04,239
Only you and I exist now.

197
00:10:12,247 --> 00:10:13,790
- I can't.
- [gasps]

198
00:10:14,333 --> 00:10:15,751
I told you.

199
00:10:16,501 --> 00:10:19,796
Beasts with a record of prior devouring
can't marry herbivores.

200
00:10:19,880 --> 00:10:21,632
I don't care about marriage.

201
00:10:21,715 --> 00:10:23,842
It's enough that we understand each other.

202
00:10:23,925 --> 00:10:25,218
Not to me, it isn't.

203
00:10:25,302 --> 00:10:28,096
I want us to build a family together.
I want kids!

204
00:10:28,180 --> 00:10:31,558
So, I just think it's inappropriate
for me to be physical with you!

205
00:10:31,642 --> 00:10:32,517
Huh?

206
00:10:32,601 --> 00:10:34,853
I turned 18 today. I'm a man now.

207
00:10:34,936 --> 00:10:36,605
- I should act like it.
- [scoffs]

208
00:10:36,688 --> 00:10:40,942
Listen. My mom and grandpa
aren't legally recognized as my family,

209
00:10:41,026 --> 00:10:43,654
so I... I get how hard all this can be.

210
00:10:43,737 --> 00:10:45,072
And I'd rather wait,

211
00:10:45,155 --> 00:10:47,532
till I've had some more time
to figure this out.

212
00:10:47,616 --> 00:10:49,660
- [growls] Stop!
- [seller] Uh, hey there?

213
00:10:51,203 --> 00:10:53,163
Can I help you folks with anything, or...

214
00:10:53,246 --> 00:10:55,082
- How much would it be for me?
- [both gasp]

215
00:10:55,165 --> 00:10:56,583
- Haru!
- How much would my meat cost?

216
00:10:56,667 --> 00:10:59,544
- Name your price and the wolf will buy it!
- What are you saying?

217
00:10:59,628 --> 00:11:02,089
I'm saying I don't understand
what you're saying.

218
00:11:02,172 --> 00:11:03,632
You've never made less sense!

219
00:11:03,715 --> 00:11:07,344
- Sorry, sir! It's just a joke.
- Really? So this is all a joke to you?

220
00:11:07,427 --> 00:11:09,304
- I'm finished!
- With what?

221
00:11:09,388 --> 00:11:11,348
- Well, if--
- Hey! It's dangerous!

222
00:11:11,431 --> 00:11:12,516
Haru! Whoa!

223
00:11:15,102 --> 00:11:17,604
You know, she actually would fetch
a pretty penny.

224
00:11:18,105 --> 00:11:18,939
Hmm.

225
00:11:21,024 --> 00:11:23,026
- [Lycaon shuddering]
- [rapid clicking]

226
00:11:26,530 --> 00:11:27,614
[Louis sighs]

227
00:11:29,699 --> 00:11:31,118
[Louis] <i>I can't concentrate.</i>

228
00:11:32,035 --> 00:11:34,162
<i>- What is he--</i>
- [rapid clicking continues]

229
00:11:35,163 --> 00:11:38,375
- [shuddering]
<i>- Ah. Meat withdrawal symptoms.</i>

230
00:11:40,210 --> 00:11:42,629
<i>- Oh, dear.</i>
- [breath trembling]

231
00:11:45,132 --> 00:11:49,386
<i>No. He would be sweating more
if that were the case.</i>

232
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:51,805
- Hey.
- Huh?

233
00:11:53,306 --> 00:11:55,684
Have a mint. It may help calm your nerves.

234
00:11:55,767 --> 00:11:56,893
- What?
- Here.

235
00:11:57,477 --> 00:11:58,728
Uh...

236
00:11:58,812 --> 00:12:01,648
Ah, right. Sorry, buddy. Thanks.

237
00:12:02,274 --> 00:12:03,233
[exclaims]

238
00:12:04,359 --> 00:12:05,444
Is that...

239
00:12:06,153 --> 00:12:07,195
Uh, the Kines?

240
00:12:10,157 --> 00:12:11,658
{\an8}[Chloe] Of course I can do it.

241
00:12:12,159 --> 00:12:13,410
But if we're found out,

242
00:12:13,493 --> 00:12:16,538
your father will let you off scot-free,
and I'd be finished.

243
00:12:16,621 --> 00:12:18,790
You understand
what I'd be putting on the line for you.

244
00:12:18,874 --> 00:12:23,086
Yes, I most certainly do, which is why
we're going to keep our mouths shut.

245
00:12:24,004 --> 00:12:25,297
[exhales]

246
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:28,175
Yeah, yeah. You're just lucky
I find it interesting.

247
00:12:29,551 --> 00:12:30,594
Hmm.

248
00:12:30,677 --> 00:12:32,304
So, this is the stuff?

249
00:12:33,722 --> 00:12:35,640
And what do you need it analyzed for?

250
00:12:35,724 --> 00:12:38,268
It's just for school. A little project.

251
00:12:38,351 --> 00:12:40,270
You're going with that? Okay.

252
00:12:41,313 --> 00:12:42,522
[sighs]

253
00:12:42,606 --> 00:12:45,358
Whatever. I'll have the results
for you next week.

254
00:12:45,942 --> 00:12:48,737
And, hey, don't forget this
when you take over.

255
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:50,447
Oh, I wouldn't dream of it.

256
00:12:50,530 --> 00:12:51,990
I'll get you a better budget.

257
00:12:52,532 --> 00:12:53,950
And maybe a smoking area.

258
00:12:54,701 --> 00:12:55,619
[chuckles]

259
00:12:56,369 --> 00:12:58,622
I'll remember that. Don't let me down.

260
00:13:01,750 --> 00:13:05,504
[Louis] <i>Why does everyone I speak to
always have to be so difficult?</i>

261
00:13:06,796 --> 00:13:08,173
[buzzing]

262
00:13:11,134 --> 00:13:12,052
[exclaims softly]

263
00:13:12,135 --> 00:13:15,013
[Louis] <i>Including her,
but in a different way.</i>

264
00:13:16,097 --> 00:13:17,807
Your visual acuity is wonderful.

265
00:13:17,891 --> 00:13:20,143
Ew! Ew! Oh, gross! I'm so scared of bugs!

266
00:13:20,227 --> 00:13:23,021
Well, that didn't stop you
from crushing it barehanded.

267
00:13:23,104 --> 00:13:25,982
You're not embarrassed
of your hunting instincts, are you?

268
00:13:26,066 --> 00:13:28,902
No, it's not that.
They really do creep me out!

269
00:13:29,402 --> 00:13:32,197
[Louis] <i>Juno and I have begun
to meet regularly for tea.</i>

270
00:13:32,906 --> 00:13:34,658
<i>Once, perhaps twice a month.</i>

271
00:13:35,367 --> 00:13:37,494
[sighs] <i>Ever since...</i>

272
00:13:39,829 --> 00:13:42,541
<i>But we never speak of it.
We never hint at it.</i>

273
00:13:43,333 --> 00:13:45,377
<i>We stick primarily to small talk.</i>

274
00:13:46,211 --> 00:13:47,170
Tell me something.

275
00:13:47,837 --> 00:13:50,048
I've been doing some thinking
and I wondered,

276
00:13:50,757 --> 00:13:52,926
you come for tea
every time if I invite you,

277
00:13:53,009 --> 00:13:55,554
but it's so hard to tell
if you even enjoy it, so...

278
00:13:56,096 --> 00:13:58,139
I can't help but wonder why.

279
00:13:58,223 --> 00:14:01,434
Just keeping up
with your youthful spontaneity, Juno.

280
00:14:01,518 --> 00:14:03,311
See, that's what I'm talking about.

281
00:14:03,812 --> 00:14:06,231
Why come if you're just going to
look down on me?

282
00:14:06,314 --> 00:14:07,941
You're 17 now, aren't you?

283
00:14:08,024 --> 00:14:10,735
An age where you want to explore
many different things.

284
00:14:11,444 --> 00:14:15,407
Things like flirting with an older guy,
or just talking to an herbivore.

285
00:14:16,032 --> 00:14:19,619
And if you can tackle both at once,
I imagine that's convenient.

286
00:14:20,161 --> 00:14:23,999
Oh! You are literally
so mean to me! [groans]

287
00:14:24,082 --> 00:14:26,877
Mean, logical, skinny.

288
00:14:27,961 --> 00:14:29,296
The more I think about it,

289
00:14:29,379 --> 00:14:32,215
the more I realize
you're not even my type to begin with.

290
00:14:32,299 --> 00:14:36,970
So, why did I end up with such a big,
stupid, idiot crush on you?!

291
00:14:37,053 --> 00:14:41,016
[Louis] <i>I don't believe this woman has
ever had an unvoiced thought in her life!</i>

292
00:14:41,099 --> 00:14:44,895
<i>It's like she can say or do
whatever she wants, and get away with it.</i>

293
00:14:44,978 --> 00:14:48,565
<i>This one girl is more terrifying
than Legoshi or the entire Shishi-Gumi!</i>

294
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:52,903
Well, to be frank,
I don't want someone like you either.

295
00:14:54,154 --> 00:14:57,866
- Come on, let's get out of here.
- What? No, we just got here.

296
00:14:57,949 --> 00:14:59,826
It's fine. 'Kay? Let's go.

297
00:15:00,493 --> 00:15:01,786
Aw.

298
00:15:01,870 --> 00:15:03,914
[mellow music playing]

299
00:15:11,755 --> 00:15:12,714
[Juno] Hey, Louis.

300
00:15:13,757 --> 00:15:16,468
You don't have
any other plans today, do you?

301
00:15:16,551 --> 00:15:17,385
I do.

302
00:15:18,053 --> 00:15:20,472
- I'm meeting my fiancée.
- Huh?

303
00:15:21,056 --> 00:15:22,474
I could have sword you knew.

304
00:15:23,224 --> 00:15:26,436
My marriage partner
was decided for me many years ago.

305
00:15:27,187 --> 00:15:29,814
She's the heiress
to another large company,

306
00:15:29,898 --> 00:15:31,775
and she's a red deer just like I am.

307
00:15:32,442 --> 00:15:34,110
- [gasps softly]
- Do you see now?

308
00:15:35,028 --> 00:15:38,114
It's true that I have no ulterior motives
in meeting with you.

309
00:15:39,366 --> 00:15:40,325
[Juno sighs softly]

310
00:15:41,117 --> 00:15:44,412
Earlier, you told me
I shouldn't be embarrassed

311
00:15:44,496 --> 00:15:46,665
about my hunting instincts, didn't you?

312
00:15:47,707 --> 00:15:51,544
Well, if you run away from me,
it'll make me want to chase you.

313
00:15:52,837 --> 00:15:54,673
I know you still think about it.

314
00:15:55,423 --> 00:15:56,800
That kiss we shared.

315
00:15:59,094 --> 00:16:01,513
<i>I saw the way
you were looking at my straw.</i>

316
00:16:03,556 --> 00:16:04,724
How I was biting it.

317
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,602
I bet you wish that was you instead.

318
00:16:08,687 --> 00:16:09,771
All worn down.

319
00:16:10,689 --> 00:16:12,399
- [Louis grunts]
- [groaning]

320
00:16:13,108 --> 00:16:14,734
Now, now, Juno.

321
00:16:14,818 --> 00:16:17,237
Big shot predators
shouldn't blush like that.

322
00:16:17,320 --> 00:16:18,363
That hurts!

323
00:16:18,905 --> 00:16:21,533
[grunts] Get away from me!

324
00:16:24,995 --> 00:16:26,287
- Bye, then.
- [Juno] Huh?

325
00:16:27,497 --> 00:16:30,458
Well, there's no way things
will work out with your fiancée.

326
00:16:30,542 --> 00:16:32,210
Not if it's an arranged marriage!

327
00:16:32,293 --> 00:16:33,795
How would you know?

328
00:16:34,379 --> 00:16:36,131
Our relationship is healthy.

329
00:16:37,048 --> 00:16:38,425
And not at all desperate.

330
00:16:40,010 --> 00:16:41,011
UDON BEBEBE

331
00:16:41,094 --> 00:16:43,847
[Juno crying]

332
00:16:45,306 --> 00:16:46,433
So, uh...

333
00:16:47,225 --> 00:16:48,685
Hey, Juno?

334
00:16:48,768 --> 00:16:50,937
Can you at least tell me
why you're crying?

335
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:55,984
We haven't seen each other in a while,
so I don't know what's going on.

336
00:16:58,611 --> 00:17:01,322
Uh... Did something happen
at the drama club?

337
00:17:01,406 --> 00:17:03,158
[crying]

338
00:17:05,118 --> 00:17:07,203
I'm impressed you tracked me down.

339
00:17:07,287 --> 00:17:09,581
Oh, everyone in the club
knows you work here!

340
00:17:09,664 --> 00:17:11,833
- Yeah, that makes sense.
- [continues crying]

341
00:17:11,916 --> 00:17:14,419
Legoshi, I had no idea
you were such a ladies' man.

342
00:17:14,502 --> 00:17:16,755
I'm not! She's a junior
from my high school drama club.

343
00:17:16,838 --> 00:17:19,424
- [Sunaga] You two suit each other.
- No, we don't-- [sighs]

344
00:17:19,507 --> 00:17:23,344
I just don't know what to do
with myself anymore. [sniffles]

345
00:17:23,428 --> 00:17:27,348
Legoshi, you're, like, the only person
I can rely on now.

346
00:17:29,267 --> 00:17:31,644
Well, I'm happy to listen,
if you wanna talk.

347
00:17:31,728 --> 00:17:32,729
But, uh,

348
00:17:32,812 --> 00:17:35,899
I don't know if I'm the best person
to be giving out advice.

349
00:17:35,982 --> 00:17:37,734
No, you're the perfect person!

350
00:17:37,817 --> 00:17:40,320
You know all about
interspecies relationships!

351
00:17:40,403 --> 00:17:41,237
Huh?

352
00:17:41,321 --> 00:17:44,365
I'm in love. And I need advice!

353
00:17:44,449 --> 00:17:48,745
This whole mess started last year,
right before the Festival of the Meteor.

354
00:17:48,828 --> 00:17:52,624
We were alone in the rehearsal room,
and I wound up pushing him to the ground.

355
00:17:52,707 --> 00:17:55,418
I really wasn't interested then,
because he wasn't my type.

356
00:17:55,502 --> 00:17:58,254
[high-speed] But after I went to visit him
on my own, it hit me.

357
00:17:58,338 --> 00:18:01,007
I couldn't stop thinking
about how beautiful Louis is.

358
00:18:01,091 --> 00:18:03,343
At the graduation ceremony,
he was all composed.

359
00:18:03,426 --> 00:18:05,595
He also had this vulnerable look
that was so gorgeous.

360
00:18:05,678 --> 00:18:08,765
And then I kissed him. But he told me
to forget about it and walked off...

361
00:18:08,848 --> 00:18:10,767
[continues indistinctly in high speed]

362
00:18:13,103 --> 00:18:16,439
{\an8}- [in normal speed] So, what do you think?
- [standby beeping]

363
00:18:16,523 --> 00:18:18,733
{\an8}Oh. Le-- Legoshi?

364
00:18:19,526 --> 00:18:21,694
{\an8}Oh, no. I think he's broken.

365
00:18:21,778 --> 00:18:23,446
{\an8}- Um... Legoshi!
- [gasps]

366
00:18:24,322 --> 00:18:28,034
Sorry. My brain wasn't able
to keep up with your plotline.

367
00:18:28,118 --> 00:18:29,786
It's okay. I blindsided you.

368
00:18:30,328 --> 00:18:32,497
I thought that might shock you
a little bit.

369
00:18:32,997 --> 00:18:35,542
If it helps any,
I'm surprised at myself too.

370
00:18:36,084 --> 00:18:38,086
It's almost embarrassing, you know?

371
00:18:38,169 --> 00:18:40,380
I didn't want to fall for Louis like this.

372
00:18:40,463 --> 00:18:43,258
[Legoshi] <i>I'm mostly surprised
that you went in for the kiss</i>

373
00:18:43,341 --> 00:18:46,386
<i>on the very same day
you realized you had feelings for him.</i>

374
00:18:47,512 --> 00:18:49,931
<i>And all this time,
I still haven't kissed Haru.</i>

375
00:18:50,515 --> 00:18:52,392
- [sighs]
<i>- Even though she...</i>

376
00:18:52,475 --> 00:18:56,354
Talking about all this has filled
my head up with his stupid face even more.

377
00:18:58,648 --> 00:19:01,484
And I guess you must have noticed
when I walked in.

378
00:19:01,568 --> 00:19:03,153
Huh? Noticed what?

379
00:19:03,236 --> 00:19:05,280
I've put on a lot of weight recently.

380
00:19:06,114 --> 00:19:09,576
Little by little, ever since
I realized I had feelings for him.

381
00:19:10,618 --> 00:19:13,955
Just thinking about him makes me
so hungry, I can barely stand it.

382
00:19:15,665 --> 00:19:17,292
It's terrifying, isn't it?

383
00:19:17,792 --> 00:19:20,003
I thought when you fell in love
with someone,

384
00:19:20,086 --> 00:19:22,172
your heart was supposed to skip a beat.

385
00:19:22,255 --> 00:19:24,174
So, why does my stomach rumble?

386
00:19:24,257 --> 00:19:25,341
[sighs]

387
00:19:26,092 --> 00:19:26,968
I think that...

388
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:31,264
somewhere deep down, I really do
just want to eat him after all.

389
00:19:32,390 --> 00:19:36,102
And it feels so shameful to mix up
love and appetite like this.

390
00:19:36,686 --> 00:19:39,731
Do you see why you're the only one
I can turn to?

391
00:19:39,814 --> 00:19:42,442
I guess. I've worried about this stuff
a lot myself--

392
00:19:42,525 --> 00:19:44,485
But I have something you don't have!

393
00:19:44,569 --> 00:19:47,447
- For me, being a carnivore is a weapon!
- Huh?

394
00:19:47,530 --> 00:19:49,115
I might be able to win him over

395
00:19:49,199 --> 00:19:51,784
with the kind of excitement
herbivore girls can't offer!

396
00:19:51,868 --> 00:19:54,621
- [chuckles nervously] Now, that's--
- Try to think about it like this.

397
00:19:54,704 --> 00:19:58,208
When you see that pipsqueak's...
[scoffs] What's her name? Uh...

398
00:19:58,291 --> 00:20:02,253
Haru's herbivorous tendencies,
it's not like they annoy you, right?

399
00:20:02,337 --> 00:20:03,838
You actually like them, right?

400
00:20:04,505 --> 00:20:06,299
Uh... Yeah, I do!

401
00:20:06,382 --> 00:20:07,634
So, you see?

402
00:20:07,717 --> 00:20:11,179
Then, don't you think
Haru feels the same about you?

403
00:20:11,262 --> 00:20:14,807
Yeah. No. I don't think
that's quite the case.

404
00:20:14,891 --> 00:20:17,977
Oh, okay. Well,
how did you win her over then?

405
00:20:18,061 --> 00:20:19,520
Sincerity?

406
00:20:19,604 --> 00:20:21,105
- Or, no. Persistence?
- Wha...

407
00:20:21,981 --> 00:20:23,524
You have to be kidding.

408
00:20:23,608 --> 00:20:25,693
Legoshi, love is a competition!

409
00:20:26,361 --> 00:20:27,904
Are you really so confident?

410
00:20:28,696 --> 00:20:30,907
You're completely assured
that Haru is yours

411
00:20:30,990 --> 00:20:33,326
with no one else
in the picture at all forever?

412
00:20:33,409 --> 00:20:36,246
What? I-- I've never really
thought about it.

413
00:20:37,205 --> 00:20:39,290
<i>Is that what made her so angry?</i>

414
00:20:40,375 --> 00:20:42,377
[parrot] Tweet-tweet! Hello there, pals!

415
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:44,629
You're on Peepee's Parrot Channel!

416
00:20:44,712 --> 00:20:46,881
And I got a question for you right here!

417
00:20:46,965 --> 00:20:49,717
About those mixed-race couples
that are all the rage these days--

418
00:20:49,801 --> 00:20:52,220
- Of course I'm for them!
- Of course you are.

419
00:20:52,303 --> 00:20:53,471
But for real, though.

420
00:20:53,554 --> 00:20:55,765
What if it was you personally?
For, against?

421
00:20:55,848 --> 00:20:57,850
- Uh...
- Not other people, but you.

422
00:20:57,934 --> 00:21:00,395
Oh, I guess it's a little awkward
to ask couples.

423
00:21:01,062 --> 00:21:02,897
You're mistaken. We're not a couple.

424
00:21:02,981 --> 00:21:04,774
What! You're not dating?

425
00:21:05,358 --> 00:21:07,443
[scoffs] Well, maybe you should start.

426
00:21:07,527 --> 00:21:11,531
Anyway, let's say a cute little herbivore
shows up, and she's hot for you.

427
00:21:11,614 --> 00:21:13,825
- For, against?
- If it's an herbivore, I don't know--

428
00:21:13,908 --> 00:21:16,703
Oh, that's a big old no, eh?
What's your reason?

429
00:21:16,786 --> 00:21:20,248
{\an8}The number one answer in our survey
right now, is "the crazy high risk."

430
00:21:20,331 --> 00:21:22,333
{\an8}Imagine you lose it
and eat your girlfriend whole.

431
00:21:22,417 --> 00:21:24,002
{\an8}- Your life's over!
- [Juno] Enough!

432
00:21:24,085 --> 00:21:26,004
I'm a grey wolf and I'm head over heels

433
00:21:26,087 --> 00:21:28,047
- for a stag right now!
- [parrot] Can I have that?

434
00:21:28,131 --> 00:21:30,466
If I worry about risk,
I'll get rejected for sure!

435
00:21:30,550 --> 00:21:32,593
- [parrot] Don't break it.
- Thought we were a couple?

436
00:21:32,677 --> 00:21:36,055
I'm sick of everyone making assumptions
about me and my life!

437
00:21:36,139 --> 00:21:36,973
Camera's expensive.

438
00:21:37,056 --> 00:21:41,269
I won't let you or anyone else
decide what will make me happy!

439
00:21:42,103 --> 00:21:44,105
[wailing]

440
00:21:52,989 --> 00:21:55,950
[Legoshi] <i>Oh, Juno. You're right.</i>

441
00:21:56,034 --> 00:21:59,454
WHAT DO YOU THINK OF THE RECENT TREND
OF INTERSPECIES RELATIONSHIPS?

442
00:21:59,537 --> 00:22:00,913
FOR - AGAINST

443
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

444
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,751
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

445
00:22:04,834 --> 00:22:08,254
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

446
00:22:09,380 --> 00:22:12,425
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

447
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,762
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

448
00:22:17,722 --> 00:22:20,933
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

449
00:22:21,017 --> 00:22:23,519
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

450
00:22:23,603 --> 00:22:26,147
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

451
00:22:27,565 --> 00:22:31,527
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

452
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:36,699
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

453
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,036
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

454
00:22:40,119 --> 00:22:44,749
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

455
00:22:44,832 --> 00:22:46,793
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

456
00:22:46,876 --> 00:22:48,002
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

457
00:22:48,086 --> 00:22:52,423
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

458
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

459
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,723
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

460
00:23:00,807 --> 00:23:02,725
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

461
00:23:02,809 --> 00:23:04,018
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

462
00:23:04,811 --> 00:23:08,731
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

463
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,608
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

464
00:23:10,691 --> 00:23:12,610
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

465
00:23:13,402 --> 00:23:16,322
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

466
00:23:17,365 --> 00:23:19,283
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

467
00:23:19,367 --> 00:23:24,163
{\an8}- <i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

468
00:23:25,373 --> 00:23:27,096
{\an8}- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>
- <i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>
